data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":318,"item_id":"fc_04de6b92baab60ea016adb42ae59188191b890dca208371663","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"TASK_INCOMPLETE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"wave-map-energy, Euclidean ambient measure source and canonical graph revision\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Continued source research and found/probed the finite-product volume formula, a possible ingredient for an explicit compact-measure proof. This gives no automatic proof that the ambient Lebesgue measure is finite on compacts; that proof and all graph edits still need to be completed. I will not claim the theorem's applicability from the presence of M013 alone, nor submit a fabricated or structurally unreviewed graph. The issue remains ordinary unfinished work, not a substantive mathematical gap.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Probe M013 MeasureTheory.volume_pi_pi (pinned module/source/commit/signature) and official EqHaar.lean lines 108–125; earlier M011/M012 probes and independent Audit A findings.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"New progress: successful M013 probe for MeasureTheory.volume_pi_pi, whose exact statement computes volume of a finite coordinate rectangle as the product of coordinate volumes; official Mathlib Constructions/Pi.lean context had already been inspected. A possible proof route is bound a compact subset of ℝⁿ inside a finite coordinate box, apply monotonicity, and compute the box volume, with the required coordinate volume and finiteness sources registered. Still not done: prove/export that ambient finite-on-compacts result, produce canonical patch set for definitions/propositions/sources/arguments and declarations, structurally check, and submit. No acceptance/Audit A PASS claimed.\\\"}\"}"}

